{
  "schema": "soveraeign.schematic/document@0.1",
  "id": "swarm-service-circuit",
  "revision": 0,
  "meta": {
    "title": "02 \u2014 Admission, bounded work, effects, and settlement",
    "status": "PROPOSED \u2014 architecture for review; no live execution",
    "notes": [
      "Logical service circuit. This drawing declares intended contracts; the editor does not implement a runtime or security sandbox.",
      "Admission checks authenticated authority, preconditions, idempotency, and available resources before recording a request and reservation.",
      "Queue and reservations form a durable admitted-work record. Capacity and budget are checked before admission and at the effect boundary.",
      "Relay dispatches admitted work. Breaker trips stop new dispatch; stopping in-flight work depends on the adapter. Reset requires separate authority.",
      "Results arrive through an authenticated observation port. Reconciliation verifies identity, attempt/version, provenance, and evidence.",
      "Settlement releases only confirmed reservations. Missing acknowledgment remains unknown and reserved pending reconciliation; never blindly retry.",
      "Refusals are recorded. Observation, cancellation, and protection ingress require capacity even when the work queue is full.",
      "One step, bounded batch, and event-driven control share these contracts; scheduling is host supplied."
    ],
    "source": "https://github.com/bdf1992/schematically",
    "timeScale": 0
  },
